Special Conditions for Electronic Advertising and Digital Boards

5 - 1 It is prohibited to place moving advertisements the content of which includes full-motion video.

5 - 2 It is permitted to place electronic or digital boards (LED) (with the exception of boards of Category (A)), and they are subject to the same conditions as other advertisements, and all the provisions of this Decree shall apply to them in respect of measurements, installation sites, rights, duties and prohibitions.

5 - 3 Special conditions for electronic or digital boards (LED):

5 - 3 - 1 (LED) boards installed on public roads where they are seen by motor vehicle drivers may display static or animated (Animation) advertisements

without their content including full-motion video, flashing or warning lights;

5 - 3 - 2 It is prohibited to convert (LED) boards into a television screen;

5 - 3 - 3 The duration of each advertisement on (LED) screens cannot be less than 8 seconds;

5 - 3 - 4 The board must be equipped with a device that adjusts the lighting in a manner that does not dazzle the eyes of drivers at night, such that the light rate does not exceed 5000 lux (lumens/ m2) in broad daylight, and 2000 lux (lumens/ m2) at night;

5 - 3 - 5 Exempted from these conditions are pharmacies, which are urged only to place the emblem of the pharmacy profession with the word "Pharmacy" without any trade name.

Licence Application

7 - 1 The licence applicant must be a commercial company or establishment duly registered, with the exception of licence applicants in the cases provided for in items /2 - 4/, /2 - 5/ and /2 - 6/ of the second Article of this Decree.

7 - 2 The application shall be submitted to the Head of the Executive Authority in the municipality within the municipal boundaries and to each of the Governor (in the central district) or the Kaymakam (in the district) outside the municipal boundaries, provided that it includes:

7 - 2 - 1 The name and capacity of its submitter, his full address, his telephone number, the real estate area in which the advertisement is intended to be placed, the property number, and a commercial circular proving that the submitter of the application is a company engaged in road advertising, subject to the provisions of item /7 - 1/ of this Article;

7 - 2 - 2 A real estate certificate for the property in which the advertisement will be placed dating back no more than three months (in the event that the sign to be installed is within private property);

7 - 2 - 3 A planning and easement certificate for the location of the sign dating back no more than three months;

7 - 2 - 4 A third-party liability insurance policy for the sign, provided that the signs are insured up to the following amounts:

-/150 000 000/ L.L. (one hundred and fifty million Lebanese Pounds) for material damages;

-/150 000 000/ L.L. (one hundred and fifty million Lebanese Pounds) for human damages;

-/750 000 000/ L.L. (seven hundred and fifty million Lebanese Pounds) total material and bodily damages per accident;

7 - 2 - 5 A document proving that the advertisement is not illuminated by means of infringement on power networks;

7 - 2 - 6 If the sign is within private property, an approval from the owner of the property registered with the Notary Public or a contract with the owner of the property duly registered with the Notary Public and the municipality within the municipal boundaries or the Kaymakamate (in the district) outside the municipal boundaries shall be attached;

If the sign is within the property of public administrations and autonomous agencies, an approval from the competent administration shall be attached, provided that this administration observes the provisions of this Decree;

If the sign is in public property within the municipal boundaries, including road setbacks not equipped with pavements, the decision shall rest with the Mayor of the municipality, subject to the provisions of this Decree and the Building Law;

7 - 2 - 1 One copy of the site map at a scale of 1/100 and of the advertising sign map at a scale of 1/20 showing the dimensions of the sign, its height above the ground, the method of its fixation and the materials from which it is made;

7 - 2 - 2 One copy of the building facade plan at a scale of 1/50 showing the lines of the building and how the advertisement is installed thereon;

7 - 2 - 3 A photograph of the site showing the road and the surrounding environment, with the obligation to indicate the actual location of the sign on the photograph;

7 - 2 - 4 In respect of signs on building rooftops (Rooftop Sign), signs of Category (D) and signs on building facades (Wall Mural) installed in the form of

{Scaffolding}, an engineering study of the structure and the chassis signed by the responsible engineer who will supervise the execution and under his responsibility must be submitted;

7 - 2 - 5 An on-demand bank guarantee in accordance with the provisions of the tenth Article of this Decree.

7 - 3 The licence application submitted to the Vehicles and Machinery Registration Department for placing advertisements on all vehicles and machinery must include:

The name and capacity of its submitter, his full address, and his telephone number if available;

A copy of the vehicle circulation permit;

A third-party liability insurance policy for the vehicle;

An undertaking drawn up before the Notary Public to respect the technical specifications provided for in item /2 - 18/ of the second Article of this Decree.

7 - 4 The Vehicles and Machinery Registration Department shall grant the licence to place advertisements on all vehicles and machinery, subject to not violating the Traffic Law and respecting the technical specifications provided for in item /2 - 18/ of the second Article of this Decree.

7 - 5 Every application that does not fulfil all the conditions provided for under this Decree, or if the licence applicant owns any sign violating the provisions of this Decree, shall be rejected.
